    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for the E.164 telephone in `OwnerTelephone.toE164`.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java`:\n\nAfter the existing 8\u201315 total-digit check, I added a `nationalLengthValid` check that enforces the national-number length against the country code:\n- `+61` (Australia) \u2192 requires exactly 9 national digits\n- `+1` (NANP) \u2192 requires exactly 10 national digits\n- other country codes are left unchecked (no spec rule for them)\n\nA number whose national part is the wrong length returns `null` from `toE164`, which `ValidateOwner` already turns into an `OwnerTelephoneInvalidException`, handled as a **400** with `{\"errors\":[\"telephone\"]}`.\n\nThis flows through the existing OfficeFloor pipeline with no new YAML/handlers needed, since the invalid-telephone path already existed.\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The new `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` test (`\"+61 123\"` \u2192 3 national digits \u2192 400) passes, and the valid `uniqueTelephone()` payload (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 9 national digits under `+61`) still passes the whole chain.",
